From the bowels of the Gag-O-Matic joke server here it is, Da Joke List FAQ!

Q: What is Da Joke List?

A: Da Joke List is a private service, maintained by LowComDom Performances, that
dispenses humor from the Gag-O-Matic joke server in Sillycon Valley California.
Most of these jokes are made from recycled ones and zeros we received in email.
Da Joke List is currently read by thousands of people. We warn you that the 
Jokes dispensed may offend you. If you are easily offended, do not join this list.

Our Basic Service:
Three Jokes per day.



Q: Okay Biff, how do I join?

A: Subscriptions are available by sending e-mail to
"da_joke_subscribe@lowcomdom.com"

In the body of your letter type:

subscribe (your email address) da_joke_list
end

You will receive a confirmation notice that you simply need to reply to, 
and then the jokes will begin.

Q: Okay, but if I ever need to How Do I Get Off This Chickenshit List?
(See I told you it might offend!)

A: If you're really not into this, or your e-mail load is too heavy, just send
a letter to "da_joke_subscribe@lowcomdom.com"

In the body of your letter type:

unsubscribe (your email address) da_joke_list
end

You will receive a confirmation notice that you simply need to reply to, 
and then the jokes will end.


Q: I can't get off this list, your software doesn't work!

A: Our spelling sucks, but our software works. There's no way all these people
from all these countries could manage to get on and off the list on a daily
basis if the software didn't work. Every time we get one of these complaints
it has ALWAYS been pilot error (Loose screw on the keyboard?). 
Here are a few things to look out for:

1) If you signed up and your company has changed your e-mail address (even 
slightly) the robot won't recognise you. You must unsubscribe with the 
email address you told the robot when you subscribed.

2) If you never signed up for our service, then it is very possible you are
receiving our jokes but not from us! Da Joke List jokes are forwarded by 
other lists to even thousands more everyday. If the people sending you the
joke didn't clean the headers of the message, it would look like 
you got it from us. There is nothing we can do about this.



Q: I just changed my email address, can you change my subscription?

A: No. Humans at LowComDom do not get involved with the list administration.
We have a robot for that. Unsubscribe from the old address and resubscribe to
the new.



Q: Do you sell the names on your list?

A: No! We HATE spam. We wish we could wipe it out. We will not sell names. It 
promotes spam, and it's not what you signed up for. You asked for jokes, that's
what your going to get, and nothing else!

Another thing to consider is who even has access to the list. We employ a robot 
to handle things for us. The robot doesn't like to share. Most of us can't even 
see who is on the list. Bill Gates could be on this list and we wouldn't know 
until Microsoft started incorporating jokes as a feature in the operating system. 
What a minute! He might be on this list! Did you see the instruction that said 
if you wanted to end your session, you go to the Start menu? When it all gets 
said a done, we don't sell the list, we don't control the list, we don't know who 
is on the list, and we don't care if the Pope or Charlie Manson is on it.



Q: Can I have fries with my jokes?

A: No.



Q: Can I submit jokes directly to the list?

A: No. Send them to us and if we like 'em, we'll pass them on.



Q: Can I have just the funny jokes, and not all the un-funny jokes?

A: They're all funny to someone.



Disclaimer: We receive jokes from a large group of sources. The only criteria
for forwarding on the Da Joke List is that we laughed when we read the joke. Da
Joke List is Proudly Politically Incorrect (we can think for ourselves), and
will publish jokes that are in danger of offending some people. If you find
yourself being overly offended by Da Joke List, just send the message to the 
robot (as described above) asking to unsubscribe. 

Don't bother telling us we're going to hell, we already know.

